---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro'
import Button from '../components/Button.astro'
import { CONTACT } from '../data/site'
import { CASHIER_PC, COMPARE, CORE_TO_SUITE, DISK_YEAR, EASY_REST, PRODUCT_ENTRY, REQUIREMENTS, SERVICE, TIERS, WHO_PAYS, rs } from '../data/pricing'
import { softwareApplication } from '../lib/jsonld'
---
<Base title="Pricing — Karots Suite" description={`Karots Suite ${rs(100000)} or Core ${rs(80000)}, once. Bugs fixed free, always; 3 months of the service plan free, then ${rs(SERVICE.monthly)} a month if you want it.`} path="/pricing/" jsonLd={[softwareApplication(Astro.site!)]}>
  <div class="wrap page">
    <h1>Pricing</h1>
    <p class="lede">Pay once for the software, and it is yours to use for as long as you like. Genuine bugs are fixed free, always. After your first 3 months, the service plan brings support, upgrades and cloud backup if you want them.</p>

    <ol class="tiers" aria-label="Plans">
      {TIERS.map((t) => (
        <li class:list={['tier', { featured: 'featured' in t && t.featured }]}>
          <h2>{t.name}</h2>
          <p class="tag">{'from' in t && t.from && <span class="unit">from </span>}<span class="n">{t.price}</span></p>
          <p class="unit">{t.unit}</p>
          <p class="for">{t.for}</p>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ol>

    <section class="block" aria-labelledby="compare">
      <h2 id="compare">Compare plans</h2>
      <div class="scroll" tabindex="0" aria-label="Plan comparison, scrolls sideways on a phone">
        <table class="compare stack">
          <colgroup><col class="what" />{TIERS.map(() => <col />)}</colgroup>
          <thead><tr><th></th>{TIERS.map((t) => <th scope="col" class:list={{ hl: t.id === 'suite' }}>{t.name}</th>)}</tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            {COMPARE.map((r) => (
              <tr>
                <th scope="row">{r.what}</th>
                {r.cells.map((c, i) => (
                  <td class:list={{ hl: TIERS[i].id === 'suite' }} data-label={TIERS[i].name}>
                    {c === true ? <span class="yes" role="img" aria-label="Yes"></span> : c === false ? <span class="no" aria-label="No">—</span> : c}
                  </td>
                ))}
              </tr>
            ))}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <ul class="know">
        <li><b>Karots Suite and Core are the software only:</b> you bring your own PC and printers, and their faults are for their seller’s warranty.</li>
        <li><b>Easy Pay</b> is a combo, not a loan: each month pays for the service you get that month. It comes to Rs. 170,000 in all over 2 years, or Rs. 125,000 over 1 year. Stopping early? Pay the rest of the Karots Suite price ({rs(EASY_REST.twoYears)} on 2 years, {rs(EASY_REST.oneYear)} on 1 year) and it’s yours, or the licence ends after written notice. Your data always stays yours.</li>
        <li><b>Complete Shop</b> is done end to end: we buy the hardware, set it all up and hand it over ready to sell. The price moves with what you choose (the PC, one 2-in-1 printer or two separate ones, a scanner, a cash drawer) and with extra cashier PCs. We quote your shop before anything is bought. If the hardware we supply breaks in the first 6 months, we sort it out.</li>
        <li><b>Putting your products in</b> is {rs(PRODUCT_ENTRY)} a product on any plan. Started with Core? Move up to Karots Suite for {rs(CORE_TO_SUITE)}; a Karots Suite shop adds plugins later for free.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="service" aria-labelledby="service">
      <div>
        <h2 id="service">Service plan</h2>
        <p class="price"><span class="n">{rs(SERVICE.monthly)}</span> <span class="once">a month</span></p>
        <p class="alt">or {rs(SERVICE.yearly)} a year</p>
      </div>
      <ul>
        {SERVICE.gets.map((g) => <li>{g}</li>)}
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="block" aria-labelledby="who-pays">
      <h2 id="who-pays">Who pays for what</h2>
      <div class="scroll">
        <table class="stack">
          <thead><tr><th></th><th>First 3 months (6 with Complete Shop)</th><th>With the plan</th><th>Without a plan</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            {WHO_PAYS.map((r) => <tr><th scope="row">{r.what}</th><td data-label="First 3 months">{r.first}</td><td data-label="With the plan">{r.plan}</td><td data-label="Without a plan">{r.none}</td></tr>)}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p>A <b>genuine bug</b> is Karots Suite doing something wrong that its guide says it does right. Problems the shop
        caused (deleted data, a virus, settings changed by someone) and faults in the PC, printer or network are charged.
        Without a plan your shop keeps working exactly as it is, and bug fixes still reach you.</p>
      <p><b>When the plan ends</b>, new cloud backups stop; the last one is kept for 30 days and we bring it back if you
        ask in that time. The backups on your own PC and USB stick carry on. The Karots catalogue is taken off your PC;
        the products you made from it stay yours. Join again any time, with nothing to pay for the months you were away.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="block" aria-labelledby="licence">
      <h2 id="licence">Your licence</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><b>One licence, one PC:</b> the main PC that runs Karots Suite. Cashier PCs and phones that connect to it need no licence of their own.</li>
        <li><b>A new PC, or a reinstall after a format:</b> tell us, and we move it free from your latest backup.</li>
        <li><b>Two PCs running it at once, or a second shop:</b> each needs its own licence.</li>
        <li><b>Your copy keeps working:</b> it needs nothing from us to keep selling. Not the internet, not a plan, not a payment check.</li>
        <li><b>Changed your mind?</b> In the first week the licence is refunded in full; after that we keep a little more each week, and after day 30 nothing is refunded.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="block" aria-labelledby="pc">
      <h2 id="pc">System requirements</h2>
      <p class="sub">The main PC, the one that runs Karots Suite:</p>
      <div class="scroll">
        <table class="req stack">
          <thead><tr><th></th><th>Minimum</th><th>Recommended</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            {REQUIREMENTS.map((r) => <tr><th scope="row">{r.what}</th><td data-label="Minimum">{r.min}</td><td data-label="Recommended">{r.rec}</td></tr>)}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p><b>Cashier PCs:</b> {CASHIER_PC}. They need no licence of their own.</p>
      <p class="small">Measured with a year of a busy shop (about 40,000 sales and 2,000 products) on PCs slowed down to
        each of these. On the minimum PC the till still finds a product in under 0.3 seconds and a year's report takes
        under 5; the recommended PC does both about twice as fast. That year took {DISK_YEAR} of disk, with a week of
        backups.</p>
    </section>

    <div class="actions">
      <Button href={`tel:${CONTACT.phone}`}>Call {CONTACT.phoneDisplay}</Button>
      <Button href={CONTACT.whatsapp} kind="ghost">Ask on WhatsApp</Button>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .page { padding-block: 2.5rem 4rem }
  .lede { margin-bottom: 2.5rem }
  .tiers { list-style: none; margin: 0 0 3rem; padding: 0; display: grid; gap: 0.75rem }
  .tier { padding: 1.25rem 1.25rem 1.4rem; border-radius: var(--r-tile); background-color: var(--surface); border: 1px solid var(--line); display: grid; align-content: start; gap: 0.2rem }
  .tier.featured { border: 3px solid var(--saffron) }
  .tier h2 { font-size: 1.3rem; margin: 0 0 0.4rem }
  .tag { margin: 0 }
  .tier .n { font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 1.2rem + 1vw, 1.9rem); white-space: nowrap }
  .unit { margin: 0; color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.95rem }
  .for { margin: 0.6rem 0 0 }
  @media (min-width: 640px) { .tiers { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr } }
  @media (min-width: 1100px) { .tiers { grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr) } }
  .compare { min-width: 44rem; table-layout: fixed }
  .compare col.what { width: 13rem }
  .compare thead th { color: var(--ink); font-family: var(--display); font-stretch: 115%; font-weight: 800; font-size: 1.05rem }
  .compare tbody th { position: sticky; left: 0; background-color: var(--bg) }
  .compare .hl { background-color: var(--saffron-soft) }
  .yes { display: inline-block; width: 1rem; height: 0.55rem; margin-top: 0.3em; border-left: 3px solid var(--paid); border-bottom: 3px solid var(--paid); transform: rotate(-45deg) }
  .no { color: var(--muted) }
  .know { margin-top: 1.5rem }
  .service h2 { font-size: 1.6rem; margin-bottom: 0.35rem }
  .price { margin: 0 0 0.25rem; display: flex; align-items: baseline; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.5rem }
  .n { font-family: var(--display); font-stretch: 115%; font-weight: 800; font-size: clamp(2rem, 1.6rem + 2vw, 2.8rem); line-height: 1.1 }
  .once, .alt { color: var(--muted) }
  ul { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; display: grid; gap: 0.55rem }
  li { padding-left: 1.7rem; position: relative }
  li::before {
    content: ''; position: absolute; left: 0.1rem; top: 0.35em; width: 1rem; height: 0.55rem;
    border-left: 3px solid var(--paid); border-bottom: 3px solid var(--paid); transform: rotate(-45deg);
  }
  .tier { padding-left: 1.25rem }
  .tier::before { content: none }
  .service { display: grid; gap: 1.25rem 3rem; padding: 1.75rem 1.5rem; border-radius: var(--r-tile); background-color: var(--ink); color: var(--bg); margin-bottom: 2.5rem }
  .service .once, .service .alt { color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--bg) 70%, transparent) }
  .service .alt { margin: 0 }
  .actions { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.75rem }
  .block { margin-bottom: 2.5rem }
  .block h2 { font-size: 1.6rem; margin-bottom: 1rem }
  .block p { margin: 1rem 0 0 }
  .block ul { gap: 0.7rem }
  .scroll { overflow-x: auto }
  table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100% }
  th, td { text-align: left; padding: 0.6rem 0.75rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); vertical-align: top; overflow-wrap: anywhere }
  thead th { font-size: 0.95rem; color: var(--muted) }
  tbody th { font-weight: 600 }
  .small { color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.95rem }
  .sub { margin: 0 0 0.75rem }
  .req tbody th { width: 9rem }
  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .stack, .compare { min-width: 0; table-layout: auto }
    .stack colgroup, .stack thead { display: none }
    .stack tr { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 0.5rem 0.75rem; padding: 0.75rem 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line) }
    .stack tbody th { position: static; grid-column: 1 / -1; width: auto; border: 0; padding: 0; font-size: 1rem; background: none }
    .stack td { border: 0; padding: 0; font-size: 0.95rem; overflow-wrap: normal }
    .stack td::before { content: attr(data-label); display: block; font-size: 0.8rem; color: var(--muted) }
    .stack .hl { background: none }
  }
  @media (min-width: 860px) {
    .service { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1.4fr; align-items: center }
  }
</style>
